& = \frac{2}{(a - b)(a - c)} + \frac{2}{(b - a)(b - c)} + \frac{2}{(c - a)(c - b)} \\
& = 0 
\end{align*}
Since this simplifies to 0, the original expression should be a constant. What is this constant? To figure this out, we can try plugging in $x=-a,-b,$ or $-c$. This gives us
